From: codebrowser deployment maintainers
Subject: Reject colon-prefixed pseudo declaration references
Upstream-base: 02e30f8f05c347b5d3831d45da7efbc3059f3c74
Reason: Clang may recover a kernel-doc field such as @pfn as the Doxygen
 declaration command @fn. Its remaining text starts with a colon and is not a
 declaration. Looking up a trailing builtin name such as "free" after parsing
 the translation unit can crash Clang Sema.
Remove-when: KDAB validates declaration-command spelling or otherwise avoids
 Sema builtin creation for these recovered kernel-doc fields.

diff --git a/generator/commenthandler.cpp b/generator/commenthandler.cpp
--- a/generator/commenthandler.cpp
+++ b/generator/commenthandler.cpp
@@ -39,4 +39,7 @@ clang::NamedDecl *parseDeclarationReference(llvm::StringRef Text, clang::Sema &S
                                             bool isFunction)
 {
-
+    Text = Text.trim();
+    if (Text.empty() || Text.starts_with(":"))
+        return nullptr;
+
     clang::Preprocessor &PP = Sema.getPreprocessor();
